(5075956, 733772, 67145, '<td valign="top">i know exactly wot you mean about losing quality when resizing for web .. i never noticed it as much as i do lately, but now after i''v put something in dpc i''ll put it back in photoshop and over sharpen it either using smart sharpen or sometimes lucisart .. that way it might look nearly sharp in dpc .. its a buggar really .. <br/>but this is brilliant .. its an excellent photograph and i love your processing .. it has a beautiful painted look .. :)<br/></td>', 'i know exactly wot you mean about losing quality when resizing for web .. i never noticed it as much as i do lately, but now after i''v put something in dpc i''ll put it back in photoshop and over sharpen it either using smart sharpen or sometimes lucisart .. that way it might look nearly sharp in dpc .. its a buggar really .. but this is brilliant .. its an excellent photograph and i love your processing .. it has a beautiful painted look .. :)', '2008-11-20 13:43:25.000000', NULL, 0),
