(5110452, 735336, 29011, '<td valign="top">Quite delighted to find this shot is yours. I didn''t get my votes in for this FS but I browsed a bunch of pics and remember this one as it stood out for me. Really like how all the elements in the shot come together. Shot could use a slight crop off the bottom but that''s my only nitpick ;) The heart on the wall is a nice touch. Hope you had an awesome trip.</td>', 'Quite delighted to find this shot is yours. I didn''t get my votes in for this FS but I browsed a bunch of pics and remember this one as it stood out for me. Really like how all the elements in the shot come together. Shot could use a slight crop off the bottom but that''s my only nitpick ;) The heart on the wall is a nice touch. Hope you had an awesome trip.', '2008-12-05 19:10:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(5111137, 733175, 3724, '<td valign="top"><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/forum.php?action=read&amp;FORUM_THREAD_ID=849392" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Archive Collection - The Posthumous Masters</a></td>', 'Archive Collection - The Posthumous Masters', '2008-12-06 00:57:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(5113550, 735211, 53147, '<td valign="top">I am always amazed by the number of people, the variety of actions, and the lack of overlapping (for the most part at least here) that you are able to capture. While I truly believe that this is a candid caught moment it is hard for me (and my take on photography as it plays out in my work and experience) to understand how this (and many of your brilliant images) is not either painstakingly  posed or a composite. Please dont take this as any kind of insult. It is far far from that. I so love and enjoy your work.</td>', 'I am always amazed by the number of people, the variety of actions, and the lack of overlapping (for the most part at least here) that you are able to capture. While I truly believe that this is a candid caught moment it is hard for me (and my take on photography as it plays out in my work and experience) to understand how this (and many of your brilliant images) is not either painstakingly  posed or a composite. Please dont take this as any kind of insult. It is far far from that. I so love and enjoy your work.', '2008-12-07 06:46:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(5118245, 733093, 37719, '<td valign="top">Simply a gorgeous photograph!</td>', 'Simply a gorgeous photograph!', '2008-12-08 21:46:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(5119317, 733452, 67152, '<td valign="top">first impressions are pretty colors and nice quaint church<br/> <br/>i agree with <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=58785" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">FocusPoint</a> on several points - the tip of the roof being cut off is a small issue that makes it feel unfinished in some way, the lack of consistency of the whites in the church give an almost dirty feel to the building, and the foreground brown strip adds little to nothing to the image<br/> <br/>In addition, the doorway being so far to the right gives it a slightly unbalanced feel.<br/> <br/>The main thing that bothers me is a lack of sharpness of focus for the Church - a bit of unsharp mask or smart sharpen makes a world of difference. <br/> <br/>It is a decent image as can be seen from the histogram of voting - squarely sitting around 5 with no high votes (8-10) and little to no low votes (1-3), but overall the image has little "wow'' factor to really draw the viewer in to stay and look.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-12-09 11:40:09.</i></td>', 'first impressions are pretty colors and nice quaint church i agree with  FocusPoint on several points - the tip of the roof being cut off is a small issue that makes it feel unfinished in some way, the lack of consistency of the whites in the church give an almost dirty feel to the building, and the foreground brown strip adds little to nothing to the image In addition, the doorway being so far to the right gives it a slightly unbalanced feel. The main thing that bothers me is a lack of sharpness of focus for the Church - a bit of unsharp mask or smart sharpen makes a world of difference.  It is a decent image as can be seen from the histogram of voting - squarely sitting around 5 with no high votes (8-10) and little to no low votes (1-3), but overall the image has little "wow'' factor to really draw the viewer in to stay and look.', '2008-12-09 11:39:47.000000', '2008-12-09 11:40:09.000000', 0),
(5120131, 729260, 56002, '<td valign="top">This is superb.  A brilliant job!</td>', 'This is superb.  A brilliant job!', '2008-12-09 16:56:47.000000', NULL, 0),
